      {
        "id": "p15-q14e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "From the above, did the order matter or did you end up with the same curve doing it either way?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The order mattered.",
          "worked": "Dilating first gives $y=2e^x+1$. Translating first gives\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2(e^x+1)\\\\y&=2e^x+2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe order mattered because the dilation doubles the upward shift when the translation comes first.",
